# The files under web/apps/web and web/packages that differ from the oracle pin (web/SOURCE), and so the ledger of how the
# stock React app departs from it. Paths are relative to web/, one per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Q-R2 allows a change only in: the auth client, the base URL and service layer, the collab provider, and branding.
# scripts/check-web-diff.sh (the `web` job of ci.yml) fails when the set of differing files is not exactly this list:
# a changed file that is not listed fails it, and so does a listed file that no longer differs. Say in the commit that
# changes a file why it falls inside Q-R2.
#
# The auth client posts JSON (issue #44, D-022, D-036), where the pin's posts a form and follows a 302. Both files are the auth client
# (Q-R2). Not changed, and still the pin's: components/account/auth-forms/unique-code.tsx, reset-password.tsx and the OAuth hook (their
# server routes are not built, so the form post they make has no JSON answer to read), and packages/services/src/auth/auth.service.ts,
# the same form-post sign-out in a service this app does not use (`@/services/auth.service` is the one `store/user` calls).
#
# the password form: a sign-in or sign-up is a JSON post, and the answer is navigated to as the 302 would have been
apps/web/components/account/auth-forms/password.tsx
# the service the sign-out menu and the password form call: `passwordAuth` is new, and `signOut` posts JSON instead of a form
apps/web/services/auth.service.ts
